---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure & Editorial Ethics"
  description="Read our full FTC affiliate disclosure and learn how Productivity Software Reviews funds independent SaaS testing while keeping editorial verdicts unbiased."
>
  <div class="prose-container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="badge">Transparency &amp; Ethics</span>
      <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        Clear, upfront disclosure on how we fund our software testing without compromising our editorial integrity.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose-section">
      <div class="card callout-card">
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          <strong>Summary (FTC Compliance):</strong> Productivity Software Reviews participates in affiliate partner programs with several SaaS providers. When you click on certain links on our site and purchase a paid subscription, we may earn a referral commission at <strong>zero extra cost to you</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>How Affiliate Links Work</h2>
      <p>
        Running real-world software benchmarks—paying for test accounts, building sample workspaces, and keeping pricing guides updated—takes significant time and resources. Rather than cluttering our pages with intrusive pop-up ads or charging readers a paywall fee, we fund our work primarily through reader referrals.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you click a link to a software tool in one of our comparison tables or verdict boxes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The price you pay never increases.</strong> You pay the exact same price (or receive a partner discount) as if you typed the vendor's URL directly into your browser.</li>
        <li><strong>Commissions come from the vendor's marketing budget,</strong> not from your invoice.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Strict Editorial Firewall</h2>
      <p>
        Reader trust is our most valuable asset. To protect the integrity of our reviews, we enforce three strict rules:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Compensation Never Dictates Verdicts:</strong> We regularly recommend free tools, open-source alternatives, and SaaS products that have no affiliate program at all whenever they are the best fit for small businesses.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Sponsored Reviews:</strong> Software companies cannot pay us to write a favorable review, remove a "Con" from a Pros &amp; Cons box, or alter their score in our comparison tables.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Clear Labeling:</strong> Every review article features a prominent disclosure notice right above the main content before you click any outbound link.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Questions?</h2>
      <p>
        If you ever have questions about our testing methodology or how a specific tool was evaluated, please reach out to us on our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header h1 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .callout-card {
    background-color: var(--bg-accent-subtle);
    border-color: #A7F3D0;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
